package server

const mcpRobloxPolicy = "Roblox Game Builder uses roblox-game-builder-v1 in bridge/browser 0.11.0, retaining the existing two MCP tools. GET /roblox/capabilities discovers GameDefinition schemaVersion:1, engineVersion:1.0.0, supported collections and bounded compiler/jobs. POST /diagrams with template:roblox-game-builder creates an ordinary flowchart document; no new diagram type or mode is introduced. diagram.game retains a strict portable typed game AST, world transforms in Roblox studs, rules, player/shared variables, inventory, quests, timers and parameterized prefabs/instances. GET/PUT /diagrams/{diagramId}/roblox inspect or atomically replace it with {baseVersion,game}. GET .../roblox/configuration returns bounded {diagramId,baseVersion,configuration:{schemaVersion,id,name,description,settings}} without collections. Combine it with every collection page at matching baseVersion values to reconstruct even an unbuildable large saved draft; discard and restart reads if any version differs. PATCH .../roblox/configuration takes {baseVersion,value:{name?,description?,settings?:partialSettings}}, preserves omitted fields, merges settings and rejects null, arrays, unknown fields and id/schemaVersion edits. It requires Read + write, canonical validation before saving and normal write recovery, returning the compact mutation summary. Collection POST/PATCH use {baseVersion,value}; omitted partial fields preserve, nested null clears optional properties and arrays replace, followed by strict resolved-game validation. Collection DELETE requires baseVersion and rejects dangling references; generic Diagram PATCH cannot bypass this namespace. Read only permits pure POST .../roblox/validate with {} or draft JSON {game}, pure POST .../roblox/preview with {steps,history?}, POST .../roblox/builds with only the current saved {baseVersion}, and exact build DELETE to cancel. These compute commands allocate no write recovery receipt. Transient builds use running/succeeded/failed/cancelled status, at most 2 active jobs, 4 retained results/32 MiB, a 120-second deadline and 15-minute TTL; lock, reload and grant revocation erase authority/results. Inspect compact /result and /artifacts metadata; /artifacts/{artifactName}?offset&limit returns encoding:base64 of at most 65536 raw bytes, byte offsets and nextOffset. Decode and concatenate bytes before UTF-8 decoding, never log private artifacts. game.rbxlx, server/client Luau, Studio importer plugin, game.json and README.txt come from the same compiler used in the UI. Unsupported fields, references, types or limits return structured 422 without partial saves. Native JSON, history and encrypted backups preserve the game definition; live collaboration rejects game documents. Publication is optional, fixed-destination and browser-UI-only: no REST/MCP publish-confirm route, credential input, arbitrary host, password, cookie or automatic retry exists. A human must configure the process-local scoped key and existing Universe/Place and review the exact digest/destination under a current explicit Read + write grant, then type a fresh one-use phrase in the local bridge's independent foreground terminal. Forged Origin/write hello claims or MCP tokens cannot provide terminal approval; no ENV/request approval exists. Non-TTY/MCP-stdio publisher startup fails closed. Preparation, terminal approval and HTTP each have a 60-second budget; denial, timeout or revocation before dispatch sends no request. A lost HTTP outcome requires Creator Dashboard version-history review and separate UI acknowledgment before another publication; no exactly-once guarantee spans browser/bridge restart. Trusted-click checks do not prove physical human intent against compromised same-origin code or a local process impersonating the browser. Local preview is not Roblox multiplayer or physics certification."
